  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Intransitive godan verb. X⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{慰|なぐさ}む, typically with ⟦{心|こころ}→心：01321_kokoro⟧ or ⟦{気|き}→気：02199_ki⟧ as the subject. The transitive pair is ⟦{慰|なぐさ}める→慰める：02133_nagusameru⟧ (to comfort someone).\n\nSomewhat literary; in everyday speech the transitive ⟦{慰|なぐさ}める→慰める：02133_nagusameru⟧ or the noun ⟦{慰|なぐさ}め→慰め：21650_nagusame⟧ is more common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{心|こころ}→心：01321_kokoro⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{慰|なぐさ}む: one's heart is soothed\n- ⟦{気|き}→気：02199_ki⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{慰|なぐさ}む: one's feelings are eased\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{慰|なぐさ}める→慰める：02133_nagusameru⟧: to comfort someone — the transitive counterpart\n- ⟦{癒|い}える→癒える：20856_ieru⟧: to heal — of a wound or grief mending over time",
